ge."],"compare":"anyOf","complexity":"O(n^2) time, O(1) space","starter":{"python":"def longestPalindrome(s):\n    # TODO: implement\n    pass\n","javascript":"/**\n * @param {*} s\n * @return {*}\n */\nvar longestPalindrome = function (s) {\n  // TODO: implement\n};\n"},"editorial":{"explanation":"Every palindrome has a centre, and there are `2n - 1` of them — `n` characters and `n - 1` gaps.\nExpand outwards from each centre while the characters match and keep the longest result.\n\n`O(n^2)` time, `O(1)` space, and far easier to get right than the `O(n^2)` DP table.\n\nManacher's algorithm reaches `O(n)` by reusing information from previous centres, which is rarely\nwhat an interviewer is after.","code":{"python":"def longestPalindrome(s):\n    best = ''\n    for center in range(len(s)):\n        for lo, hi in ((center, center), (center, center + 1)):\n            while lo >= 0 and hi < len(s) and s[lo] == s[hi]:\n                lo -= 1\n                hi += 1\n            candidate = s[lo + 1:hi]\n            if len(candidate) > len(best):\n                best = candidate\n    return best\n","javascript":"var longestPalindrome = function (s) {\n  let best = '';\n  const grow = (lo, hi) => {\n    while (lo >= 0 && hi < s.length && s[lo] === s[hi]) {\n      lo--;\n      hi++;\n    }\n    const candidate = s.slice(lo + 1, hi);\n    if (candidate.length > best.length) best = candidate;\n  };\n  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n    grow(i, i);\n    grow(i, i + 1);\n  }\n  return best;\n};\n"},"complexity":"O(n^2) time, O(1) space"}}
